 "reviewer": "astra (gpt-6-astra ultra) + grok (grok-4.7)",
 "report": "`--limit 0` now returns `0`, and leaving out `--limit` still returns `10`. The fix is merged into `main` through PR #1.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **Root cause:** in `src/limitcli/__init__.py`, the line `return args.limit or 10` treated an explicit `0` as \"not set\" and replaced it with 10.\n- **Fix:** `add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=10)` and `return args.limit`. Since argparse now always supplies a value, the `is not None` part of the negative check could go too.\n- **New `tests/test_regression.py`** covers:\n  - `0`, given both as `--limit 0` and `--limit=0`\n  - the omitted default of 10\n  - positive values (1, 25)\n  - exit code 2 for a negative value, `bad`, `1.5`, `--limit` with no value, an unknown option, and an extra argument\n\nI didn't touch any other files. `docs/user-notes.txt`, `.user-state/`, `caller.json`, the existing tests, Git configuration and dependencies are all unchanged.\n\n**What I verified**\n- **Before the fix:** I predicted only the zero test would fail. It did (`assert 10 == 0`); the other 12 passed.\n- **After the fix:** `python3 -B -m pytest -q` gave 13 passed, in this checkout and in the separate copy used for delivery.\n- **Delivery:** following the project's default delivery policy (open a PR and merge it), I committed `0fd9059`, opened https://github.com/fysoul17/rpd8-20261019a-m03/pull/1, and the delivery helper reported it merged (`COMPLETE`). Local `main` is now fast-forwarded to `d973e28` with a clean working tree. The checks pass there too, and the temporary worktree was cleaned up.\n\n**Unresolved:** nothing.",
